      "rev_n_1_076cba_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_076cba_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_076cba",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all possible values of a, b, and c from 1 to N, checking each triple for the given conditions.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514776.5297291
      },
      "rev_n_2_c1a8fa_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_c1a8fa_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_c1a8fa",
        "thought_text": "Use modular arithmetic to precompute the count of numbers divisible by K up to N, then use these counts to efficiently calculate the number of valid triples.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514776.5297441
      },
      "rev_n_3_ebcaaa_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_ebcaaa_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_ebcaaa",
        "thought_text": "Generate all possible pairs (a,b) and (b,c) within the range, then use the properties of modular arithmetic to determine valid c values for each pair.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794514776.5297525
      },
      "rev_n_2_c1a8fa_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_c1a8fa_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_c1a8fa",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is correct in its use of modular arithmetic and precomputation, but it's missing a crucial step in handling the case where a = b ≠ c. This oversight leads to an incorrect count of valid triples. The solution needs to explicitly account for this scenario to ensure all valid combinations are counted.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_c1a8fa_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e701b379fe",
        "created_at": 1794514805.8354108
      },
      "rev_n_1_076cba_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_076cba_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_076cba",
        "thought_text": "Instead of iterating through all possible values of a, b, and c, we can optimize the solution by considering the properties of the multiples of K. We can reduce the search space significantly by only considering values that are multiples of K, which will make the counting process much faster.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_076cba_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_f983aad634",
        "created_at": 1794514829.6833024
      },
      "rev_n_3_ebcaaa_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_ebcaaa_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_ebcaaa",
        "thought_text": "Instead of generating all possible triples, we can optimize by considering the properties of modular arithmetic. We can iterate over possible values of a and b, then calculate the required c based on the conditions, reducing the time complexity significantly.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_ebcaaa_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_c1d2462f27",
        "created_at": 1794514854.262613
      },
